[gd_scene load_steps=10 format=3]

; The Book form of the rock: a book.
;
; "Un libro pequeno, encuadernado en cuero pardo y atado con una correa.
; Los cantos de las hojas estan dorados y manchan los dedos."
;
; So: a small book in brown leather, tied shut with a strap, its leaves
; gilt at the edge. It stands on the stone the rock was, and it is
; heavier than a book of that size should be - which is the seam, and it
; is the same seam the stone has in the other truth.

